From 0c2f38fc48c67e275b5d9403ddfaf79e1f012387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:26:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(v2): reuse verified connected bytes for bounded block
 chunks

Keep one runtime-owned verified body under an exact chain/profile/tip/root/revision/invalidity/body/context stamp. Every chunk call still checks access, observes authority once, refuses recovery or paused state and enforces the current full-body cap. Clear old entries before replacement and publish no new cache entry on failed loads or ranges. Preserve full ReadConnectedBody and detached previously connected reads.

Route readblock through bounded slices and recheck its complete in-memory authority after Status, which can silently fault the runtime. Retain existing invalid_request range and empty EOF behavior. Per-call body-load-attempt/cache-hit/copy diagnostics have no validation influence.

Focused runtime and extracted production ReadBlock tests pass. Coverage includes one actual validation across many exact-wire chunks, smaller hit caps, cold failure no-install, pending/paused/fault guards, all stamp fields and real source-restoration ABA. The adapter injects a genuine runtime sync fault from its Status callback; removing only the post-Status fence reproduces stale publication. It does not execute whole Node::Status or start a node.
